<body>
    <h1>Gold Layer Naming Standards</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h1 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-Purpose">Purpose</h1>
<p>This document defines the naming conventions for all&nbsp;<strong>Gold L=
ayer (Curated / Consumption ready)</strong> data objects built within the A=
llianz ADP Lakehouse using Databricks Delta Lake.<br>
  The Gold layer is the <strong>semantic presentation layer</strong>, servi=
ng enterprise reporting, MI, analytics, pricing, actuarial, underwriting, o=
perational BI, and downstream integrations.<br>
  These naming standards ensure:</p>
<ul>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"e=
d3d1f23-aa3b-400b-b24d-3bee8d79b195">Business-friendly, <strong><span style=
=3D"color:#c9372c;">Az UK EDM</span>-aligned</strong> naming</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"a=
c88f1f5-b4fc-4732-bcb1-ec437135075b">Consistent naming of facts, dimensions=
, bridges, aggregates, audits</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"c=
d644b7c-2bc6-4199-aded-f639f6e0cddc">Clear lineage across multi-source harm=
onisation</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"8=
ea778f8-2573-4ab9-8a6c-37751d64f57d">Predictability for BI/AI consumers and=
 external vendors</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"0=
ca8b1b2-55a3-4f3f-a637-591146cab2c8">Ease of onboarding for legacy data pla=
tform decom/migration teams</li>
</ul>
<p><br>
  These standards are <strong>project-agnostic</strong> and apply to all fu=
ture ADP development.</p>
<div role=3D"region" aria-label=3D"Note" class=3D"confluence-information-ma=
cro  confluence-information-macro-note">
 <span role=3D"presentation" class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-=
warning confluence-information-macro-icon"></span>
 <div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
  <p>These naming standards represent the <strong>target</strong> for all n=
ew Gold layer models in the ADP platform.<br>
    For the SAS Decommissioning &amp; Migration Project:</p>
  <ul>
   <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D=
"687c2913-f033-4ebc-b48a-ebfa5d85051b">Where existing SAS interfaces/ extra=
cts feed downstream processes that cannot be changed, <strong>Gold outputs =
may retain legacy structures</strong> <em>only for interface protection</em=
>.</li>
   <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D=
"0c7ce8d1-2b17-4667-80fb-299e1acfdf82">Any such exceptions must be document=
ed in the SAS decom decision log</li>
   <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D=
"011b87e4-6674-4d63-8ab4-78cc25324fc8">All redesigned assets, mart replacem=
ents, conformed dimensions, and new facts/dimensions <strong>must follow th=
is naming standard</strong>.</li>
  </ul>
 </div>
</div>
<p><br></p>
<h1 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-Scope">Scope</h1>
<p>These conventions apply to all Gold layer objects:</p>
<h3 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-PhysicalTables"><strong>Physical Tables<=
/strong></h3>
<ul>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"b=
d4d4f69-3d1b-41af-bd2c-01c57b1a4783">Fact tables (<code>fct_=E2=80=A6</code=
>)</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"e=
d923f11-46f3-443c-b123-c804eaa6b9a8">Dimension tables (<code>dim_=E2=80=A6<=
/code>)</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" style=3D"color=
:#c9372c;" data-uuid=3D"06e2e9fb-d121-4ebc-8535-865b9fe99885"><span style=
=3D"color:#c9372c;">Bridge tables (<code>brg_=E2=80=A6</code>)</span></li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"7=
35e8241-e93f-40b1-810d-e688142dbd7a">Aggregation tables (<code>=E2=80=A6_ag=
g</code>)</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"b=
467d231-7210-45cb-b71d-9e86d0d2636a">Reference dimensions</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"e=
17c4d57-801d-4e91-baef-c340cc87b044">Snowflaked dimensions</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-Attributes(Columns)"><strong>Attributes =
(Columns)</strong></h3>
<ul>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"0=
647f381-6885-482e-8086-96cb82f3a672">All use <strong>Subject + Qualifier + =
LogicalDataType [refer&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://cmp.allianz.net/pages/viewpa=
ge.action?pageId=3D1753831232#InstandaProductDataConfigurationandGovernance=
-DataAttributeNamingConvention" rel=3D"nofollow">naming standards</a>]</str=
ong></li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"7=
73caba0-439d-48d3-965e-960e020c32d7">PascalCase</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"1=
87b09e2-aaf2-4617-903c-17800c1d838b">Business-friendly</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-Views"><strong>Views</strong></h3>
<ul>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"0=
11fa9ca-e0cf-4a03-82db-57db9bd169c4">Insert views: <code>vw_ins_&lt;source&=
gt;_&lt;target&gt;</code></li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"5=
9575464-1e07-4c6a-b43a-41482b4fda4c">Presentation views</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-Auditcolumns"><strong>Audit columns</str=
ong></h3>
<ul>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"c=
c5fddb2-c747-4a04-978f-9f8e393bec48"><code>DWH_DATA_DTS</code></li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"3=
d2a2352-65ea-40ee-87a6-7ca5307f8799"><code>DWH_CREATE_DTS</code></li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"6=
6120999-d1dd-4bc8-bbaf-61bd2d2e3114"><code>DWH_REC_SRC_CD</code></li>
</ul>
<p><br>
  Not in scope:</p>
<ul>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"9=
25f9442-f371-402d-b847-966b2e55556d">Raw Vault, Business Vault, ODS, or DV2=
.0 naming (covered in separate pages)</li>
</ul>
<h1 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-Conceptual&amp;LogicalDataModelNamingSta=
ndards"><strong>Conceptual &amp; Logical Data Model Naming Standards</stron=
g></h1>
<h2 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-2.1AttributeNamingConvention"><strong>2.=
1 Attribute Naming Convention</strong></h2>
<p>Gold attributes must:</p>
<ul>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"1=
81ac31e-f23c-4abf-840a-1fad6f7891db">align to the <span style=3D"color:#c93=
72c;"><strong>AZ UK EDM</strong></span></li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"9=
6f4acac-502a-4369-9432-c319a63248ea">use <strong>business semantics</strong=
>, not source semantics</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"8=
d57547d-385c-43d1-9cee-fc099a61cce9">harmonise multi-source input fields</l=
i>
</ul>
<h1 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-2.3NamingRuleSets"><strong>2.3 Naming Ru=
le Sets</strong></h1>
<h2 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-2.3.1CommonRules"><strong>2.3.1 Common R=
ules</strong></h2>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"5a3624c1-b063-4e45-83d4-7d7807ab208e"><span style=3D"colo=
r:#172b4d;"><a href=3D"https://cmp.allianz.net/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=
=3D1753831232#InstandaProductDataConfigurationandGovernance-DataAttributeNa=
mingConvention" rel=3D"nofollow">https://cmp.allianz.net/pages/viewpage.act=
ion?pageId=3D1753831232#InstandaProductDataConfigurationandGovernance-DataA=
ttributeNamingConvention</a></span></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"1a1d8e1b-e9d6-4f06-b833-1a475e6eb87e">Shareable across bu=
siness</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"07bfce59-d8d2-460b-a967-ed2f6b538da9">No system-specific =
wording</li>
 <li style=3D"color:#c9372c;" data-uuid=3D"3573b046-5ff9-4374-9337-ee9b0744=
9857"><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Acronyms only if industry-standard (IS=
IC, VAT..)</span></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-2.3.2LogicalAttributeNaming(GoldLayer)">=
<strong>2.3.2 Logical Attribute Naming (Gold Layer)</strong></h2>
<p><br>
  All columns must use:</p>
<ul>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"c=
5fbca7d-ea86-4326-bd60-f9c52892e052">Business terminology</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"f=
e4bb776-ce35-4e62-ac0a-10debc5f0836">
  <p>Unabbreviated terms preferred</p></li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"c=
d83e393-5679-40fa-8d68-89275ea86a03">
  <p>Align with glossary names where possible</p></li>
</ul>
<p><br></p>
<h2 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-2.3.3PhysicalRuleSet(Databricks)"><stron=
g>2.3.3 Physical Rule Set (Databricks)</strong></h2>
<h3 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-Tables"><strong>Tables</strong></h3>
<ul>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"9=
9e30a40-5130-4b55-8733-723a4d957ecb">Lowercase names</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"a=
ec147c7-059a-4662-a37a-cf64f21de9cf">Prefixes applied (<code>dim_</code>, <=
code>fct_</code>, <code>brg_</code>)</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"1=
d21de4b-2e32-4712-be15-67685cf6ea26">Words separated by underscores</li>
</ul>
<p><br></p>
<h1 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-2.4LogicalObjectsinGoldLayer"><strong>2.=
4 Logical Objects in Gold Layer</strong></h1>
<h2 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-2.4.1DataModel"><strong>2.4.1 Data Model=
</strong></h2>
<p><br>
  Represented as dimensional models (facts, dimensions, bridges).</p>
<h2 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-2.4.2SubjectArea"><strong>2.4.2 Subject =
Area</strong></h2>
<ul>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"c=
84775b4-cec7-4e18-825d-f05b704ae740">Policy</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"8=
802e02e-c4ea-4c0b-b3ee-6e1b50c3da6f">Customer</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"3=
270f02c-9b4c-4327-acb1-00cdc62fcdb1">Claims</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"1=
b4aba27-934e-4a18-96aa-4d2a9ac596b7">Pricing</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"f=
a3df4bc-6d84-42b5-997c-8b6200b32882">Booking</li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-2.4.3Entities"><strong>2.4.3 Entities</s=
trong></h2>
<ul>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"6=
e6fc260-cf7a-4ac9-9c86-7a225b4b6469">Dim_ tables represent entities</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"a=
9495866-e08e-4ed3-9ec4-afa6dfb8f617">Fact tables represent business events/=
measures</li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-2.4.4LogicalViews"><strong>2.4.4 Logical=
 Views</strong></h2>
<p><br>
  Used for semantic presentation models</p>
<h2 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-2.4.5Attribute"><strong>2.4.5 Attribute<=
/strong></h2>
<p><br>
  Follows SubjectQualifierLogicalDataType</p>
<h2 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-2.4.6Relationship"><strong>2.4.6 Relatio=
nship</strong></h2>
<p><br>
  Verb phrases like:</p>
<ul>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"5=
9b75958-ce65-405f-8792-300597a29ead">Policy <strong>has</strong> InsuredEnt=
ity</li>
 <li class=3D"___ccc16d0 fje8fi8 f1ng9h0j f1bwykku f18jd3zf" data-uuid=3D"e=
72ee1ae-48f9-4613-9d07-c1aaec7b9962">Customer <strong>owns</strong> Policy<=
/li>
</ul>
<h1 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-3PhysicalDataModelNamingStandards"><stro=
ng>3 Physical Data Model Naming Standards</strong></h1>
<h1 id=3D"GoldLayerNamingStandards-3.1TableNamePrefixes"><strong>3.1 Table =
Name Prefixes</strong></h1>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"relative-table confluenceTable" style=3D"width: 70.4855%;"=
>
  <colgroup>
   <col style=3D"width: 9.72841%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 38.7278%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 14.1898%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 15.739%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 21.6305%;">
  </colgroup>
  <tbody class=3D"">
   <tr class=3D"">
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh"><strong>Object Type</strong></th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh"><strong>Definition</strong></th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh"><strong>Prefix</strong></th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh"><strong>Example Table Name</strong></th>
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh"><strong>Example </strong></th>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh"><strong>Fact Table</strong></th>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">A fact table contains <em>measures</em> and =
<em>foreign keys</em> to dimensions. It represents a <strong>business event=
</strong>, <strong>transaction</strong>, <strong>snapshot</strong>, or <str=
ong>process</strong> at a defined grain. Facts answer questions like <em>=
=E2=80=9CWhat happened?=E2=80=9D</em> or <em>=E2=80=9CHow much?=E2=80=9D</e=
m>.</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><code>fct_</code></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><code>fct_policy_premium</code></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Stores premium-related measures for each pol=
icy at the chosen grain (e.g., per policy per transaction).</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh"><strong>Dimension Table</strong></th>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">A dimension table defines <strong>business e=
ntities</strong>, providing <strong>context</strong> and descriptive attrib=
utes that enrich fact tables. Dimensions answer <em>=E2=80=9CWho?=E2=80=9D<=
/em>, <em>=E2=80=9CWhat?=E2=80=9D</em>, <em>=E2=80=9CWhere?=E2=80=9D</em>, =
<em>=E2=80=9CWhen?=E2=80=9D</em> questions. Includes surrogate/hash key, at=
tributes, and audit fields.</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><code>dim_</code></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><code>dim_customer</code></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Holds customer-related attributes (PolicySta=
rtDate, ClaimsStatusCode, etc.) used to filter, group, and join facts.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh"><strong>Bridge Table</strong></th>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">A bridge table resolves <strong>many=E2=80=
=91to=E2=80=91many relationships</strong> between a fact and a dimension or=
 between two dimensions. Used when a fact links to multiple dimension value=
s, or where two dimensions have many-to-many relationships.</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><code>brg_</code></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><code>brg_rating_quote_result</code></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Connects rating quotes to multiple underwrit=
ing results (many=E2=80=91to=E2=80=91many). Contains RatingQuoteKey, UndwgR=
esultKey, audit fields, and optional context attributes.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh"><strong>Aggregation Table</strong></th>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">An aggregation table stores <strong>pre=E2=
=80=91summarised metrics</strong> for improved performance and ease of use.=
 Helps reduce compute on large fact tables by presenting business-level sum=
maries (daily, monthly, policy-level, etc.).</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><code>&lt;subject&gt;_agg</code></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><code>policy_premium_agg</code></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Contains pre-aggregated premium totals by po=
licy, time period, and product to speed up reporting and analytics.</td>
   </tr>
   <tr class=3D"">
    <th class=3D"confluenceTh"><strong>Insert View</strong></th>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Insert views generate the <strong>Gold layer=
 target structure from Silver</strong>, applying cleansing, conforming, sur=
rogate key generation, and audit population. One insert view is created per=
 source feeding a Gold entity.</td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><code>vw_ins_&lt;source&gt;_&lt;target&gt;</=
code></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><code>vw_ins_rad_dim_rating_quote</code></td=
>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Loads <code>dim_rating_quote</code> from Rad=
ar Silver tables, applying hashing, transformations, and DWH audit columns.=
</td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<p><br></p>
